From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:07:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 44/99] v8: e2k: schedule across rare branches by what is live
 at the deoptimization exit

A rare branch (compare + rbranch in one wide command) used to end the
scheduling window: nothing given after it could go into its command or
above, because the layer did not know what the code at its target reads.
In hot loops nearly every window ended this way.

RareBranchScope now takes a mask of the registers that are live at the
target. For a deoptimization check these are the registers that are
never allocated (but for the scratch ones) and the register inputs of
the instruction, which is all a translation can name. What follows the
check may be scheduled into its command or above it if the target
cannot tell: it is no store, no transfer of control, writes no live
register or flag, and loads only from the frame at a known offset (any
other address may be valid only because the check passed). Other rare
branches (deferred code, stack checks) keep everything live.

The compare of a rare branch writes its own scratch predicate, the
command of a linked rare branch does not move when something joins
above it, and the continue label after a deoptimization check is bound
only when something refers to it, so that it does not close the window.

mjsunit default, stress, jit_fuzzing, --always-osr, --gc-stress and
always_sparkplug: the same failures as before the change.
